    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a high-ceiling lineup anchored by **Gunnar Henderson**, who earns our premier start with an 81.87 score. His matchup against Lugo creates an ideal environment; the combination of a significant park boost (+16%) and a favorable platoon edge (+14%) outweighs the minor efficiency penalty imposed by the opponent\u2019s ability to hold runners. Following closely are **Kyle Tucker** (75.35) and **Jacob Wilson** (71.63), both of whom capitalize on soft opposing xERAs. **Jacob Wilson** particularly benefits from a dynamic platoon advantage against Schultz, while **Kyle Tucker** remains a staple start even in neutral platoon conditions due to his elevated base projection and the clear SP skill mismatch.\n\nWe are aggressively leveraging speed-to-base potential today, specifically with **Josh Lowe** and **Jackson Merrill**. Both players see their scores buoyed by the \"Slow SP Delivery\" factor against Bradley, adding critical value to our scarcity-focused build. The most difficult personnel decision involved leaving **Brayan Rocchio** and **Miguel Vargas** on the bench; while **Miguel Vargas** boasts an elite xwOBA of 0.403, his 56.21 score simply couldn't crack the top-tier efficiency metrics required to displace **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** or **Josh Jung** in today's high-leverage spots. Conversely, **Denzer Guzman** was an easy exclusion, falling well below our 40-point floor due to a bottom-of-the-order assignment that suppresses his scoring potential.\n\nRisks remain, specifically regarding **Drake Baldwin** and **Liam Hicks**. **Drake Baldwin** faces a moderate 50.65 projection, hindered by a wind-in factor (-5%) that suppresses his base power. **Liam Hicks** carries the lowest score of our starting nine (43.10), as his plate appearance value is significantly eroded by a negative platoon dynamic (-11%) against Cantillo. While these two represent the weak links of the day, their inclusion remains necessary to navigate our positional requirements while keeping the core bats like **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** and **Heliot Ramos** in optimal slots to maximize run production.",
